{#
 # A surface.
 #
 # A plain card is the default: a rule around a section of a page. `elevated` is the one that adds
 # something — borderless, set apart by the tuned `$box-shadow` — and it is what a card standing for
 # a whole page wears. Asking for it rather than opting out of it is the point: what adds style
 # should be spelled out, and a card nested in another that forgot to say so no longer stacks a
 # second shadow on the first.
 #
 # `tone` names what the card means, the way `Badge`'s does. `muted` is a card the member may read
 # but not act on — the identity block the club owns; `primary` singles one card out of a series,
 # the season being validated among the seasons before it. Untoned is the default and paints nothing.
 #
 # The parts are their own components (`Card:Header`, `Card:Body`, `Card:Footer`) rather than a
 # fixed shape, because the call sites differ too much inside: a body with no padding around a
 # table, two headers, a `list-group-flush` in place of a body.
 #}
{% props elevated = false, tone = null %}

{%- set card = html_cva(
    base: 'card',
    variants: {
        elevated: { true: 'border-0 shadow' },
        tone: {
            muted: 'bg-body-tertiary border-0',
            primary: 'border-primary',
        },
    },
) -%}

{%- set classes = card.apply({ elevated: elevated, tone: tone }|filter(v => v is not null)) -%}

<div{{ attributes.defaults({ class: classes }) }}>
    {% block content %}{% endblock %}
</div>
